%W:Far from the cry of the city, where flowers pretty caress the streams,
%W:Cozy to hide in, to love side-by-side in. Don't let it abide in my dreams.
%W:
%W:[Chorus]
%W:
%W:Picture you upon my knee, just tea for two and two for tea, 
%W:Just me for you and you for me, alone!
%W:
%W:Nobody near us, to see us or hear us, 
%W:No friends or relations on weekend vacations,
%W:We won't have it known, dear, that we have a telephone, dear. 
%W:
%W:Day will break and you'll awake and start to bake 
%W:A sugar cake for me to take for all the boys to see.
%W:We will raise a family, a boy for you, a girl for me, 
%W:Oh, can't you see how happy life would be?
%W:
%W:You are revealing a plan so appealing I can't help but falling for you,
%W:Darling, I planned it; can't you understand it is yours to command it, so do.
%W:All of your schemes I'm admiring, they're worth desiring but can't you see,
%W:I'd like to wait there for some future date dear; 
%W:it won't be too late, dear, for me.

